      "content": "The pattern you're describing is a cycle, not a personal failing, and recognizing the pattern is the first, most courageous step toward changing it. The \"point\" isn't about achieving some perfect, permanent state of \"better,\" but about learning to navigate the difficulty without letting the cycle completely consume you. Instead of seeing it as a binary of success or failure, perhaps you can view each moment as a data point—a chance to learn something new about your triggers. You are not destined to fail; you are in a difficult process that requires strategy and self-compassion, not self-punishment.",
      "source": "target",
